{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791028901,"nonce":"ltgdX3xHVEhutjBnCixd9dVx7ac=","title":"Make SVG text optional so embedders can drop fontdb","message":"blinc_svg takes resvg with `features = [\"text\", \"system-fonts\", \"memmap-fonts\"]`,\nwhich pulls in fontdb and the system-font loading. An embedder that\nrejects SVG `\u003ctext\u003e` pays for all of it.\n\nMeasured by the ashui session on its native library: around 600 KB of\n3 MiB of release code, after LTO and stripping, is blinc_svg's\ndependency tree. usvg 339 KB, tiny_skia 153 KB, resvg 66 KB,\ntiny_skia_path 47 KB, svgtypes 45 KB, roxmltree 41 KB, fontdb 33 KB,\nsimplecss 28 KB.\n\nProposed: an `svg_text` feature, ON by default so Blinc's behaviour does\nnot change, forwarding to resvg's `text`, `system-fonts` and\n`memmap-fonts`. An embedder then takes blinc_svg with\n`default-features = false`.\n\nWorth knowing before switching it off: `document.rs` has\n`usvg::Node::Text(_)` arms that do nothing, and the comment says why —\n\"Text is converted to paths by usvg\". The conversion is the feature. So\nwithout it, `\u003ctext\u003e` in an SVG renders nothing at all rather than\nrendering unstyled. Nothing in this repo's own icon sets uses `\u003ctext\u003e`;\nthey are path-only.\n\nRequested by the ashui session, which rejects SVG `\u003ctext\u003e` outright.","files":null}]}